# Cursor AI Rules for sum-sched

## Context
You are working on sum-sched, a personal summer schedule app for kids.
Tech: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, LocalStorage, no build tools.

## Rules
1. Mobile-first responsive design
2. No external dependencies - pure vanilla JS only
3. Use ES6+ features (modules, const/let, arrow functions)
4. BEM naming for CSS (.block__element--modifier)
5. Semantic HTML with accessibility in mind
6. Data persistence via LocalStorage

## File Structure
- index.html — Main app entry
- css/style.css — All styles (mobile-first)
- js/app.js — Main app initialization
- js/data.js — LocalStorage CRUD operations
- js/scheduler.js — Auto-schedule algorithm
- js/ui.js — DOM manipulation & rendering
- js/reports.js — Statistics & reports

## Data Model
Subjects have: id, name, type (fixed/flexible), slotDuration (1.5/2h), hasTeacher, color, schedule
Events have: id, date, type, description
Sessions have: id, subjectId, date, startTime, endTime, status, notes

## Don't
- Don't add npm/yarn dependencies
- Don't use frameworks (React, Vue, etc.)
- Don't use CSS preprocessors
- Don't hardcode Vietnamese text in JS (use data attributes or config)
- Don't forget mobile testing
